{% section-card tone="intro" %}
## What is retrieval-augmented generation?

**Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG)** combines information retrieval with language generation. Before an LLM answers, the application retrieves relevant documents and places them in the model's context so the answer can use current, private, or domain-specific evidence.

In plain language: RAG gives an LLM an open-book reference for each question. It improves grounding without retraining the model and can attach sources to claims.

| Without RAG | With RAG |
| --- | --- |
| Knowledge stops at the model's training cutoff. | Indexed information can be refreshed continuously. |
| Facts may be hallucinated. | Answers can be grounded in retrieved passages. |
| Private domain data is unavailable. | Authorized private data can enter the request context. |
| Updating knowledge may require fine-tuning. | Updating the index does not retrain the model. |
{% /section-card %}

{% topology-lab dataFile="/api/content/genai/rag-systems/data/rag-request-topology.json" /%}

{% section-card %}
## Types of RAG systems

{% accordion defaultOpen="basic" %}
{% accordion-item id="basic" title="Basic RAG" %}
- **Workflow:** User Query -> Vector Search -> Retrieve Documents -> Generate Answer

Basic RAG is simple, fast, and architecturally clear. Its limits are weak relevance filtering, bounded context, and little multi-step reasoning. It fits documentation search, simple Q&A, and basic chatbots.
{% /accordion-item %}
{% accordion-item id="conversational" title="Conversational RAG" %}
- **Workflow:** Conversation History -> Query Rewriting -> Vector Search -> Context-aware Generation

This form preserves follow-up context and creates natural conversations, but adds state, token cost, and query-rewriting complexity. It fits support and interactive assistants.
{% /accordion-item %}
{% accordion-item id="agentic" title="Agentic RAG" %}
- **Workflow:** Query Analysis -> Tool Selection -> Multi-step Retrieval -> Reasoning and Synthesis

An agent decides what to retrieve and may use several sources. It supports complex, multi-hop questions but increases latency, cost, and failure modes. It fits research and analysis workflows.
{% /accordion-item %}
{% accordion-item id="self-rag" title="Self-RAG" %}
- **Workflow:** Generate Initial Answer -> Self-critique -> Retrieve if Needed -> Refine Answer

The model decides whether evidence is needed and critiques its own output. This can improve fact-critical work, but remains expensive and complex.
{% /accordion-item %}
{% /accordion %}
{% /section-card %}

{% section-card tone="warn" %}
## Common RAG challenges

{% accordion defaultOpen="relevance" %}
{% accordion-item id="relevance" title="Retrieval relevance" %}
- **Problem:** retrieved documents do not answer the question.

Common causes are weak embeddings, poor chunking, and inadequate query understanding. Improve it with stronger embeddings, hybrid vector-plus-keyword search, query expansion, and reranking.

{% code-block file="/api/content/genai/rag-systems/code/query-expansion.js" language="javascript" title="Query expansion" /%}
{% /accordion-item %}
{% accordion-item id="hallucination" title="Hallucination control" %}
- **Problem:** the model adds unsupported claims.

Use explicit grounding instructions, citations, confidence handling, and fact-verification layers.

{% code-block file="/api/content/genai/rag-systems/code/grounded-prompt.js" language="javascript" title="Grounded prompt" /%}
{% /accordion-item %}
{% accordion-item id="context" title="Context-window management" %}
- **Problem:** over-retrieval exceeds the model's context budget.

Use deliberate chunking, summarization, relevance filtering, and iterative retrieval.

{% code-block file="/api/content/genai/rag-systems/code/context-prioritization.js" language="javascript" title="Context prioritization" /%}
{% /accordion-item %}
{% accordion-item id="latency" title="Response latency" %}
- **Problem:** embedding, retrieval, reranking, and generation run sequentially.

Parallelize independent work, cache embeddings, stream output, and precompute document summaries.

{% code-block file="/api/content/genai/rag-systems/code/parallel-rag.js" language="javascript" title="Parallel RAG processing" /%}
{% /accordion-item %}
{% /accordion %}
{% /section-card %}

{% section-card %}
## RAG system demo

The demo simulates retrieval, evidence-backed generation, source attribution, and confidence display. It does not call an external model or database.

{% interactive-block id="genai/rag-systems" /%}
{% /section-card %}

{% section-card %}
## Implementation progression

{% accordion defaultOpen="simple" %}
{% accordion-item id="simple" title="Simple retrieve-then-generate" %}
Embed the question, retrieve the top matching passages, join them into a context, and instruct the model to answer only from that context.

{% code-block file="/api/content/genai/rag-systems/code/simple-rag.js" language="javascript" title="Simple RAG" /%}
{% /accordion-item %}
{% accordion-item id="production" title="Production RAG" %}
Production systems rewrite follow-up questions, combine vector and keyword retrieval, rerank results, enforce a token budget, stream output, cache useful context, and convert operational failures into useful responses.

{% code-block file="/api/content/genai/rag-systems/code/production-rag.js" language="javascript" title="Production RAG" /%}
{% /accordion-item %}
{% accordion-item id="advanced" title="Agentic multi-step RAG" %}
Agentic RAG plans a retrieval strategy, invokes the appropriate search or calculation tools, records failed steps, and synthesizes the successful evidence.

{% code-block file="/api/content/genai/rag-systems/code/agentic-rag.js" language="javascript" title="Agentic RAG" /%}
{% /accordion-item %}
{% /accordion %}
{% /section-card %}

{% section-card %}
## RAG evaluation

| Layer | Metrics and tests |
| --- | --- |
| Retrieval | Precision@K, Recall@K, mean reciprocal rank, and NDCG |
| Generation | Faithfulness, answer relevance, context precision, and human review |
| Business | End-to-end latency, cost per query, user satisfaction, and task completion |
| Test strategy | Golden Q&A datasets, A/B tests, regression tests, and load tests |
{% /section-card %}

{% section-card %}
## Production best practices

| Area | Practice |
| --- | --- |
| Architecture | Parallelize retrieval, cache embeddings and common queries, balance vector replicas, and degrade gracefully. |
| Monitoring | Track query patterns, relevance scores, user feedback, latency, and cost. |
| Security | Filter documents by user authorization, sanitize inputs and outputs, log access, and redact PII. |
| Optimization | Batch work, tune chunk size and overlap, rerank results, and A/B test prompts. |

- Better retrieval usually beats retrieving more documents.
- Start with basic RAG and add conversational or agentic behavior only when needed.
- Measure retrieval quality separately from answer quality.
- Design explicitly for empty retrieval, conflicting sources, provider failure, and unsupported claims.
{% /section-card %}

